<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rudolf I of Burgundy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 859–912</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rudolf I, of the Welf family, was the first king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-burgundy">Upper Burgundy</a>. After the fall of the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-fat">Charles the Fat</a> in 888 he was crowned at the abbey of Saint-Maurice d'Agaune, ruling the lands between the Jura and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pennine-alps">Pennine Alps</a> around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-geneva">Lake Geneva</a>. He failed in his attempt to win Lotharingia but kept his kingdom, which passed to his son Rudolf II.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rudolf-i-of-burgundy.jpg" alt="Rudolf I of Burgundy" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Furfur · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vertrag_von_Verdun_und_Ribemont.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
